course: dictionary
lesson: 6645
title: Nudge: a small, gentle push
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A nudge is a small, gentle push. When you meet the word, read the words around it. In «If some of those differences help an animal survive and raise more young, the next generation has a little more of them, and over thousands of generations small nudges add up to big changes», the clues are "small" and "add up". Each nudge is a tiny change, and many of them together make a big one.
explain: Nudge can also be a verb. To nudge someone is to push them gently, often with your elbow, to get their attention. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "small gentle changes add up to big changes" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Nudge is never a hard shove. Whether it is a push, a reminder or a gentle encouragement, the feeling is always small and gentle. If you are not sure, ask yourself: is this a big strong push, or a little one?
fact: To nudge someone is to push them gently, usually with your elbow, to get their attention.
fact: To nudge something is to move it a little by pushing it gently.
fact: To nudge someone towards something is to gently encourage them to do it.
fact: A nudge is a small push or a gentle reminder, as in «a gentle nudge».
fact: «Prices are nudging ten pounds» means prices are getting close to ten pounds.
exercise: In class, a friend gives you a nudge when the teacher asks a question. What does a nudge mean here? | A loud shout across the room | A long letter from the teacher | *A small push to get your attention | A gift for a good answer
exercise: «She nudged the cup a little closer to me.» What does nudged mean? | Ran around it fast | Knocked it over completely | Painted it bright blue | *Moved it a little by pushing gently
exercise: «Prices are nudging ten pounds.» What does nudging mean here? | Falling to zero | Costing exactly fifty pounds | Being given away free | *Coming close to ten pounds
test: «Over thousands of generations, small nudges add up to big changes.» What does small nudges mean here? | Long holidays | Huge sudden shocks | *Tiny, gentle changes | Loud noises
test: An app sends Ravi a reminder to drink water. The app is giving him what? | A loud alarm | A long letter | A heavy shove | *A gentle nudge
exam: Which sentence uses nudge to mean gently encourage someone to do something? | *Her coach nudged her gently towards trying out for the team | The team ran around the field twice | Her coach shouted loudly at the goalkeeper | The bus nudged past the school gates
